Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 11:18:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] fix(upload): validate file MIME type, drop SVG, bound
 memory usage
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- SVG uploads were allowed based on extension alone; SVG is executable
  content served as image/svg+xml, so a crafted file could run scripts when
  opened or embedded (stored XSS / content spoofing).
- The filter checked only the filename extension, so a renamed executable
  (evil.exe -> evil.png) passed. It now requires the declared MIME type to
  match the extension category, failing closed.
- uploadMedia allowed 10 x 50MB in memory per request (~500MB peak). Reduced
  to 6 x 25MB to bound per-request memory (multer memory storage).

Tests: server/src/middleware/upload.test.ts - accepts matching
image/video/audio; rejects SVG, renamed executables, mismatched MIME, and
unsupported extensions.

Run: cd server && npx jest src/middleware/upload.test.ts

